le is a large village in south-eastern Botswana, about 50 kilometres north-west of Gaborone, and the administrative centre of Kweneng District.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/moliere"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/moliere.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Molière</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Molière, the stage name of Jean-Baptiste Poquelin, was a French playwright and actor, regarded as the greatest master of French comedy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/molina-de-aragon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/molina-de-aragon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Molina de Aragón</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Molina de Aragón is a town on the Gallo river in the province of Guadalajara, Spain, dominated by one of the largest castles in the country.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/molise"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/molise.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Molise</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Molise is a region of southern Italy, between Abruzzo, Lazio, Campania and Apulia, with its capital at Campobasso.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/molla-panah-vagif"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/molla-panah-vagif.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Molla Panah Vagif</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Molla Panah Vagif was an Azerbaijani poet and statesman who served as vizier of the Karabakh Khanate under Ibrahim Khalil Khan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/molly-brant"><span class="enc-name">Molly Brant</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Molly Brant was a Mohawk leader of the 18th century, the consort of the British Indian superintendent Sir William Johnson and the elder sister of Joseph Brant.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/molly-malone"><span class="enc-name">Molly Malone</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">&quot;Molly Malone&quot;, also known as &quot;Cockles and Mussels&quot; or &quot;In Dublin's Fair City&quot;, is a song set in Dublin that has become the city's unofficial anthem.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/molokans"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/molokans.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Molokans</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Molokans are a Russian Spiritual Christian sect that emerged in the 18th century and rejects the Orthodox Church's priesthood, icons and sacraments.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/molokai"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/molokai.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Molokaʻi</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Molokaʻi is one of the main Hawaiian Islands, lying between Oʻahu and Maui.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/moloku-kie-raha"><span class="enc-name">Moloku Kie Raha</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">Moloku Kie Raha, the &quot;four mountains of Maluku&quot;, was the traditional name for the four Muslim kingdoms of the North Moluccas: Ternate, Tidore, Bacan and Jailolo.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/molopo-river"><span class="enc-name">Molopo River</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Molopo River is a mostly dry river of southern Africa that rises near Mahikeng and flows west towards the Orange River.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/molossians"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/molossians.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Molossians</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Molossians were the leading tribe of ancient Epirus, in north-western Greece, around Dodona and the Ioannina basin.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/molotov-ribbentrop-pact"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/molotov-ribbentrop-pact.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Molotov–Ribbentrop Pact</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · 1939</span><span class="enc-snip">The Molotov–Ribbentrop Pact was the non-aggression treaty signed by Nazi Germany and the Soviet Union in Moscow on 23 August 1939.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/molpoi"><span class="enc-name">Molpoi</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Molpoi were a guild of singers at Miletus devoted to the cult of Apollo Delphinios.</span></a></li></ul>
